1
00:00:38,539 --> 00:00:41,959
MY BIAS, MY BOSS

2
00:00:43,252 --> 00:00:45,545
Luni, what does it mean
if someone gives you a bottle of wine

3
00:00:45,546 --> 00:00:47,798
and says it's from her heart?

4
00:00:49,049 --> 00:00:51,718
In fact, that wine is said
to help one's love come true.

5
00:00:52,177 --> 00:00:54,263
That means more than interest.

6
00:00:54,596 --> 00:00:56,973
It's normally used
to express a head-on romance.

7
00:00:56,974 --> 00:01:00,184
A head-on romance?

8
00:01:00,185 --> 00:01:03,564
That woman definitely likes you.

9
00:01:08,986 --> 00:01:10,070
CHAN

10
00:01:17,536 --> 00:01:20,581
Da-reum, I'll be out of town
for a few days from tomorrow.

11
00:01:20,998 --> 00:01:24,001
Could we meet up at least
for a moment before I leave?

12
00:01:27,629 --> 00:01:28,714
So she

13
00:01:29,715 --> 00:01:30,924
likes me?

14
00:02:05,751 --> 00:02:07,960
Let's go. I'll walk you home.

15
00:02:07,961 --> 00:02:09,378
No, thank you.

16
00:02:09,379 --> 00:02:12,715
I need to stop by somewhere.
I'll go by myself.

17
00:02:12,716 --> 00:02:16,135
But still, I should walk you...

18
00:02:16,136 --> 00:02:18,472
Mr. Kang, are you okay?

19
00:02:19,264 --> 00:02:20,807
Of course, I'm fine.

20
00:02:21,308 --> 00:02:22,601
Why wouldn't I be?

21
00:02:23,310 --> 00:02:24,769
You seem a little off.

22
00:02:24,770 --> 00:02:26,063
Your face is all red.

23
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:32,234
- Just go away.
- What?

24
00:02:32,235 --> 00:02:34,737
I take back walking you home.
It's canceled.

25
00:02:34,738 --> 00:02:35,822
Go on already.

26
00:02:36,657 --> 00:02:37,658
Bye.

27
00:02:38,200 --> 00:02:41,995
Okay, I'll be going then.

28
00:02:49,169 --> 00:02:50,253
Goodbye.

29
00:03:01,598 --> 00:03:03,808
This one is obviously way heavier.

30
00:03:03,809 --> 00:03:05,602
Same amount, my foot.

31
00:03:06,311 --> 00:03:09,189
How come my own mother
cares more about Ha-gi than me?

32
00:03:09,856 --> 00:03:10,982
It's ridiculous.

33
00:03:19,324 --> 00:03:20,367
What on earth?

34
00:03:21,201 --> 00:03:22,619
Why is a girl
coming out of this house?

35
00:03:23,662 --> 00:03:25,914
Tell me. Who is she?

36
00:03:26,289 --> 00:03:28,165
Why would your employee come
all the way to your house?

37
00:03:28,166 --> 00:03:29,876
And what's with those romantic eyes?

38
00:03:30,711 --> 00:03:33,546
I had an urgent proposal to finish.
She was here to help. Happy now?

39
00:03:33,547 --> 00:03:36,216
She looked familiar, though.

40
00:03:38,677 --> 00:03:40,177
The nosebleed! The big ice ball!

41
00:03:40,178 --> 00:03:42,305
She's that crazy drunk girl, right?

42
00:03:43,849 --> 00:03:46,142
So she works for you now?

43
00:03:46,143 --> 00:03:47,269
Mind your own business.

44
00:03:50,272 --> 00:03:51,982
Is that wine?

45
00:03:52,566 --> 00:03:54,735
So much for work.
You two are totally a thing.

46
00:03:55,235 --> 00:03:58,029
I didn't set it up.
She brought it over

47
00:03:58,280 --> 00:03:59,488
saying it was from her heart.

48
00:03:59,489 --> 00:04:01,700
Wait, so she confessed to you?

49
00:04:06,246 --> 00:04:07,247
Well...

50
00:04:07,873 --> 00:04:09,540
She hasn't said it out loud.

51
00:04:09,541 --> 00:04:12,794
Mr. Kang, have this and cheer up.

52
00:04:13,420 --> 00:04:14,504
Good luck.

53
00:04:17,090 --> 00:04:20,593
But she sneaks up to cheer me on.

54
00:04:20,594 --> 00:04:21,762
Mr. Kang!

55
00:04:24,306 --> 00:04:25,557
I'll move next to you.

56
00:04:27,017 --> 00:04:28,894
She randomly puts her hands on me.

57
00:04:30,061 --> 00:04:31,271
Oh, man.

58
00:04:31,730 --> 00:04:32,731
Above all...

59
00:04:37,611 --> 00:04:38,945
She smiles at me
every time she sees me.

60
00:04:41,865 --> 00:04:44,868
She must have feelings for me, right?

61
00:04:46,745 --> 00:04:47,788
No.

62
00:04:50,040 --> 00:04:51,041
At that point...

63
00:04:52,709 --> 00:04:54,419
it's love.

64
00:04:55,712 --> 00:04:56,713
What...

65
00:04:57,964 --> 00:04:59,132
Love?

66
00:05:01,843 --> 00:05:02,928
Love.

67
00:05:06,473 --> 00:05:07,474
Love.

68
00:05:17,442 --> 00:05:20,237
COULD WE MEET UP AT LEAST
FOR A MOMENT BEFORE I LEAVE?

69
00:05:22,697 --> 00:05:25,449
LEE CHAN OFFICIAL
HAS STARTED A LIVE STREAM

70
00:05:25,450 --> 00:05:28,453
TUNE IN RIGHT NOW!

71
00:05:29,788 --> 00:05:31,998
Hi. It's been a while, right?

72
00:05:33,583 --> 00:05:36,461
I have an early start tomorrow,
so I can't stay long.

73
00:05:38,213 --> 00:05:39,256
I went live

74
00:05:39,923 --> 00:05:42,509
because I just wanted to see you,
even if it was like this.

75
00:05:44,678 --> 00:05:48,056
I can't see you, but you can see me.

76
00:05:52,185 --> 00:05:54,271
There's something
I wanted to tell you in person.

77
00:05:55,522 --> 00:05:56,982
I might have hurt you

78
00:05:57,524 --> 00:05:59,442
because I wasn't careful at times

79
00:06:00,068 --> 00:06:02,320
but thank you
for always supporting me.

80
00:06:03,488 --> 00:06:05,949
That's how I truly feel.

81
00:06:12,831 --> 00:06:14,583
I read in my favorite book

82
00:06:15,750 --> 00:06:18,253
that sincerity eventually
shines through over time.

83
00:06:19,921 --> 00:06:22,257
I hope my sincerity
reaches you as well.

84
00:06:29,097 --> 00:06:30,515
Gosh, it's late.

85
00:06:30,765 --> 00:06:32,559
I should go to bed now.

86
00:06:34,019 --> 00:06:35,312
I'll be back. Bye.

87
00:06:38,565 --> 00:06:39,566
THE LIVE STREAM HAS ENDED

88
00:06:47,782 --> 00:06:49,700
DA-REUM

89
00:06:49,701 --> 00:06:52,995
Chan, I'm afraid
I don't have time today.

90
00:06:52,996 --> 00:06:54,164
Let's catch up later.

91
00:06:54,748 --> 00:06:57,584
And I'm okay
with what happened that day.

92
00:06:57,876 --> 00:06:59,336
Please don't let it bother you.

93
00:07:01,796 --> 00:07:03,423
Thanks for texting me back, Da-reum.

94
00:07:04,549 --> 00:07:05,967
Have a safe trip to your shoot.

95
00:07:06,217 --> 00:07:07,344
I'll be rooting for you from afar.

96
00:07:09,137 --> 00:07:10,764
I'LL BE ROOTING FOR YOU FROM AFAR

97
00:07:25,362 --> 00:07:28,156
APPELLO

98
00:07:28,323 --> 00:07:29,616
Get a grip, Kang Ha-gi.

99
00:07:30,158 --> 00:07:31,284
Act normal.

100
00:07:33,078 --> 00:07:34,496
Just keep it normal.

101
00:07:56,977 --> 00:07:57,978
Thank

102
00:07:59,229 --> 00:08:00,271
you...

103
00:08:01,022 --> 00:08:03,274
Mr. Kang, did you find
any more stickers at home?

104
00:08:03,942 --> 00:08:05,902
Yesterday felt like a treasure hunt.
It was really fun.

105
00:08:06,361 --> 00:08:08,196
- If you find more...
- Ms. Nam.

106
00:08:08,530 --> 00:08:09,614
Yes?

107
00:08:09,864 --> 00:08:11,241
We're at work.

108
00:08:13,284 --> 00:08:14,368
I'm the CEO.

109
00:08:14,369 --> 00:08:15,370
CEO

110
00:08:16,121 --> 00:08:17,204
And you're an employee.

111
00:08:17,205 --> 00:08:18,206
EMPLOYEE

112
00:08:19,082 --> 00:08:20,708
Keep your personal

113
00:08:20,709 --> 00:08:21,710
and work life

114
00:08:21,960 --> 00:08:23,003
separate, okay?

115
00:08:38,101 --> 00:08:39,102
Goodness.

116
00:08:44,232 --> 00:08:46,775
The doors are closing.

117
00:08:46,776 --> 00:08:48,861
Wait, Mr. Kang!

118
00:08:48,862 --> 00:08:50,447
Mr. Kang, let me...

119
00:08:52,574 --> 00:08:53,908
What was that about?

120
00:08:55,035 --> 00:08:56,619
What's wrong with him
this early in the morning?

121
00:08:58,329 --> 00:09:00,123
Did I mess up again?

122
00:09:06,671 --> 00:09:08,590
Excuse me. Sorry.

123
00:09:10,133 --> 00:09:11,592
The CEO is going to call me in a bit.

124
00:09:11,593 --> 00:09:13,428
Make some room, please.

125
00:09:13,678 --> 00:09:14,804
Why would he call you?

126
00:09:15,221 --> 00:09:17,431
Why else? Look at that.

127
00:09:17,432 --> 00:09:20,143
The K-Wave project is worth
a massive 1.5 billion won.

128
00:09:21,102 --> 00:09:23,062
- Check this out.
- Oh, really?

129
00:09:23,063 --> 00:09:24,064
K-SWEETNESS
TO SATISFY YOUR 5 SENSES!

130
00:09:24,355 --> 00:09:26,940
"A Dalgona keychain
that tastes sweet when you lick it."

131
00:09:26,941 --> 00:09:28,942
Is this really the best
an adult could come up with?

132
00:09:28,943 --> 00:09:30,028
It's a 100 percent fail.

133
00:09:31,654 --> 00:09:34,074
If you carry that around,
it's totally going to attract bugs.

134
00:09:35,075 --> 00:09:36,326
I hope it works out.

135
00:09:36,868 --> 00:09:38,828
- What's with that look?
- Let's start the meeting.

136
00:09:41,873 --> 00:09:43,457
K-WAVE PROJECT
INTERNAL CONTEST RESULTS

137
00:09:43,458 --> 00:09:44,666
We took internal submissions

138
00:09:44,667 --> 00:09:47,587
for the K-Wave project hosted
by the Korea Heritage Service, right?

139
00:09:47,796 --> 00:09:49,756
Today, I'll announce the winner.

140
00:09:50,423 --> 00:09:51,591
Since there's only one spot

141
00:09:51,841 --> 00:09:53,425
for the fashion category
in this project

142
00:09:53,426 --> 00:09:55,470
the choice of item was crucial.

143
00:09:55,762 --> 00:09:56,930
The chosen idea is

144
00:09:58,515 --> 00:09:59,516
Lee...

145
00:10:04,646 --> 00:10:06,481
Min-a's Mosaic Bojagi.

146
00:10:11,444 --> 00:10:12,487
- Congrats!
- Congratulations.

147
00:10:13,613 --> 00:10:15,030
- Sit back down.
- Sit down quickly.

148
00:10:15,031 --> 00:10:16,199
Min-a, congratulations.

149
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:18,909
This is awesome.

150
00:10:18,910 --> 00:10:20,537
Ms. Min-a, please come up
and walk us through it.

151
00:10:21,121 --> 00:10:22,288
Yes, sir.

152
00:10:25,792 --> 00:10:27,043
Incredible!

153
00:10:34,342 --> 00:10:36,052
Hello.

154
00:10:36,302 --> 00:10:39,139
I'm Lee Min-a, a new hire
on the Merchandising...

155
00:10:42,225 --> 00:10:43,893
- Team.
- She's nervous.

156
00:10:46,437 --> 00:10:47,604
Well...

157
00:10:47,605 --> 00:10:50,983
My proposed item is the Mosaic Bojagi

158
00:10:50,984 --> 00:10:53,777
inspired by the traditional
patchwork wrapping cloth.

159
00:10:53,778 --> 00:10:57,614
The plan is to collaborate
with Geosang fabric shop in Jongno

160
00:10:57,615 --> 00:11:00,451
which has been around
for three generations.

161
00:11:02,328 --> 00:11:04,830
The patchwork wrapping cloth

162
00:11:04,831 --> 00:11:07,958
closely resembles mosaics
and stained glass.

163
00:11:07,959 --> 00:11:11,379
I expect it to feel familiar
to international customers too.

164
00:11:12,505 --> 00:11:13,630
It's so pretty.

165
00:11:13,631 --> 00:11:14,799
That's all. Thank you.

166
00:11:16,050 --> 00:11:17,051
Awesome!

167
00:11:19,470 --> 00:11:23,016
Marketing and Merchandising
will work on this project together.

168
00:11:23,266 --> 00:11:24,267
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

169
00:11:38,990 --> 00:11:41,534
What's that? It's so cute.

170
00:11:42,744 --> 00:11:44,786
A fan of mine drew this character.

171
00:11:44,787 --> 00:11:46,164
It's so cute
that I've got it all memorized.

172
00:11:46,748 --> 00:11:48,374
What's this supposed to be, though?

173
00:11:48,625 --> 00:11:49,959
A bear or a pig?

174
00:11:52,587 --> 00:11:55,589
Good point. It has a pig's nose

175
00:11:55,590 --> 00:11:58,343
- but a bear's ears.
- I'd say it's a pig.

176
00:12:01,262 --> 00:12:02,639
They're looking for the styling team.

177
00:12:03,139 --> 00:12:05,183
- Okay, we'll head over.
- Thanks.

178
00:12:07,268 --> 00:12:09,020
- Chan.
- Oh, thank you.

179
00:12:10,230 --> 00:12:13,024
I honestly don't know where you'd be
without that photo book.

180
00:12:13,650 --> 00:12:16,444
What makes it so special that you
carry it around like a lucky charm?

181
00:12:17,070 --> 00:12:18,738
It just...

182
00:12:21,574 --> 00:12:22,575
makes me feel better.

183
00:12:25,995 --> 00:12:28,456
Whenever I doubt myself

184
00:12:28,998 --> 00:12:31,834
wondering if I should
continue with this career

185
00:12:32,210 --> 00:12:33,544
or if people will still love me...

186
00:12:35,880 --> 00:12:38,716
this book cheers me on to keep going.

187
00:12:39,175 --> 00:12:41,427
The fan who made this
probably has no idea

188
00:12:41,928 --> 00:12:43,846
that it became
your most treasured item.

189
00:12:45,265 --> 00:12:46,849
I don't think she's still my fan.

190
00:12:47,475 --> 00:12:48,851
It's been ten years.

191
00:12:50,687 --> 00:12:52,105
True, so much time has passed.

192
00:12:52,397 --> 00:12:55,066
Who stays that devoted
for such a long time?

193
00:12:56,150 --> 00:12:59,070
I adored you for 12 years.
I can tell that much.

194
00:12:59,320 --> 00:13:01,906
You are a good person.

195
00:13:02,198 --> 00:13:05,410
If you tried to be
a good person so far

196
00:13:05,785 --> 00:13:08,788
that alone makes you a good person.

197
00:13:14,585 --> 00:13:15,795
Actually, there is.

198
00:13:16,379 --> 00:13:17,547
There's one.

199
00:13:19,757 --> 00:13:22,885
SE CORPORATION

200
00:13:26,764 --> 00:13:29,017
What are SE's cars doing here?

201
00:13:31,769 --> 00:13:34,605
No way. Just a moment, please.

202
00:13:35,857 --> 00:13:38,150
GEOSANG FABRIC SHOP

203
00:13:38,151 --> 00:13:39,609
Thank you
for making the right decision.

204
00:13:39,610 --> 00:13:40,653
My pleasure.

205
00:13:42,322 --> 00:13:43,323
Sir.

206
00:13:46,075 --> 00:13:47,993
Hello, Ms. Lee.

207
00:13:47,994 --> 00:13:50,538
What's going on here?

208
00:13:51,247 --> 00:13:53,874
You remember we're signing
the contract today, right?

209
00:13:53,875 --> 00:13:55,460
Well, the thing is...

210
00:13:55,918 --> 00:13:58,670
Listen, I'm sorry.

211
00:13:58,671 --> 00:14:03,343
SE brought us a similar offer first.

212
00:14:04,218 --> 00:14:06,261
And their terms were far better.

213
00:14:06,262 --> 00:14:08,056
But sir.

214
00:14:08,556 --> 00:14:10,724
I showed you

215
00:14:10,725 --> 00:14:12,727
this Mosaic Bojagi
before anyone else.

216
00:14:13,144 --> 00:14:14,937
How could SE possibly know...

217
00:14:15,855 --> 00:14:17,190
Ideas can

218
00:14:18,649 --> 00:14:20,568
overlap, can't they?

219
00:14:20,735 --> 00:14:21,736
Excuse me?

220
00:14:25,573 --> 00:14:28,575
Ms. Nam? That's none of your concern.

221
00:14:28,576 --> 00:14:29,952
The operations team
will take care of it.

222
00:14:31,454 --> 00:14:32,455
What?

223
00:14:42,173 --> 00:14:43,174
I'm sorry.

224
00:14:45,510 --> 00:14:48,053
Canceling on the day of the contract?
That makes no sense.

225
00:14:48,054 --> 00:14:49,680
They even snatched our workshop.

226
00:14:49,889 --> 00:14:52,891
It seems they're trying to block us
from bidding altogether.

227
00:14:52,892 --> 00:14:55,644
We've been backstabbed by SE
way too many times.

228
00:14:55,645 --> 00:14:57,938
At this rate,
it's definitely an inside job.

229
00:14:57,939 --> 00:14:59,773
We need to root them out, sir.

230
00:14:59,774 --> 00:15:02,109
Are you suggesting
there's a spy among us?

231
00:15:02,110 --> 00:15:04,695
- What other explanation is there?
- Listen.

232
00:15:05,488 --> 00:15:06,531
I also had...

233
00:15:07,949 --> 00:15:09,200
the same thought for a while.

234
00:15:10,993 --> 00:15:12,161
But my conclusion was

235
00:15:12,912 --> 00:15:15,540
not to recklessly suspect
my own Appello people.

236
00:15:20,461 --> 00:15:23,922
Right now, winning this bid is
what matters most.

237
00:15:23,923 --> 00:15:26,591
Everyone, focus on coming up
with a backup item.

238
00:15:26,592 --> 00:15:27,676
- Yes, sir.
- Gosh.

239
00:15:27,677 --> 00:15:29,594
The deadline is in ten days.

240
00:15:29,595 --> 00:15:31,556
- My Dalgona keychain...
- Let's stop here.

241
00:15:32,473 --> 00:15:34,558
But the Dalgona...

242
00:15:34,559 --> 00:15:36,017
- We don't have much time...
- I'm sorry.

243
00:15:36,018 --> 00:15:37,311
I apologize.

244
00:15:51,617 --> 00:15:52,618
COCOTALK

245
00:15:58,833 --> 00:16:00,668
LEE CHAN'S SCHEDULE CHAT

246
00:16:00,918 --> 00:16:03,838
LEE CHAN'S SCHEDULE FOR DECEMBER

247
00:16:16,517 --> 00:16:18,686
Before makeup today.

248
00:16:19,395 --> 00:16:20,813
I'll still push through.

249
00:16:22,398 --> 00:16:23,858
Is she busy?

250
00:16:25,193 --> 00:16:27,153
DA-REUM

251
00:16:33,075 --> 00:16:34,285
She has such a nice smile.

252
00:16:48,007 --> 00:16:50,634
Mr. Kang, you should go home today.

253
00:16:50,635 --> 00:16:52,093
You pulled an all-nighter
yesterday too.

254
00:16:52,094 --> 00:16:53,262
Not until we find a backup item.

255
00:16:53,554 --> 00:16:56,265
If SE snatches the K-Wave project
along with their platform launch

256
00:16:56,641 --> 00:16:57,766
we'll lose all our investors.

257
00:16:57,767 --> 00:16:59,643
Then, maybe we should revisit

258
00:16:59,644 --> 00:17:00,936
- my Dalgona...
- Are you kidding me?

259
00:17:00,937 --> 00:17:04,065
Read the room, for crying out loud.
You're being such a nuisance.

260
00:17:04,273 --> 00:17:06,399
Young-woo, any updates
on the traditional boxes?

261
00:17:06,400 --> 00:17:09,194
The wooden lacquer box makers aren't
producing any because the lacquer

262
00:17:09,195 --> 00:17:10,820
- won't dry in the winter.
- Yes.

263
00:17:10,821 --> 00:17:12,697
And the mother-of-pearl boxes
are way over our budget.

264
00:17:12,698 --> 00:17:13,741
How about the binyeo hairpins?

265
00:17:14,033 --> 00:17:15,701
They're already working
with another company.

266
00:17:17,578 --> 00:17:19,037
How did it go
with the Korean paper hanji?

267
00:17:19,038 --> 00:17:21,331
They refused to collaborate.

268
00:17:21,332 --> 00:17:23,959
So, every single vendor
on this list said no?

269
00:17:23,960 --> 00:17:26,462
What now? We're never going
to make the deadline at this rate.

270
00:17:27,171 --> 00:17:28,965
All right. Even so

271
00:17:29,090 --> 00:17:30,466
let's keep trying
until we find a way.

272
00:17:30,716 --> 00:17:32,300
- Yes, ma'am.
- Okay.

273
00:17:32,301 --> 00:17:33,302
Ms. Nam.

274
00:17:33,719 --> 00:17:34,720
Where did you get this?

275
00:17:35,513 --> 00:17:36,556
Pardon?

276
00:17:36,847 --> 00:17:37,848
This keychain.

277
00:17:42,645 --> 00:17:45,397
My mom knows the apprentice
of this master knot artisan.

278
00:17:45,398 --> 00:17:47,316
She got it from her.

279
00:17:47,567 --> 00:17:48,776
MASTER KNOT ARTISAN
IM CHEONG-RIM

280
00:17:49,151 --> 00:17:53,072
The colors and designs are amazing.

281
00:17:53,322 --> 00:17:54,781
- Right.
- I agree.

282
00:17:54,782 --> 00:17:55,825
How do we get in touch?

283
00:17:56,617 --> 00:17:59,870
The master is practically
living in seclusion

284
00:18:00,204 --> 00:18:02,790
so even if we go to see her,
it might not work.

285
00:18:03,040 --> 00:18:06,002
My mom said she'd ask the apprentice.

286
00:18:07,086 --> 00:18:09,130
- Please...
- This has to work.

287
00:18:23,060 --> 00:18:24,352
CEO KANG HA-GI OF APPELLO

288
00:18:24,353 --> 00:18:25,895
I'll be outside your place
tomorrow morning.

289
00:18:25,896 --> 00:18:27,314
Pack for a business trip and meet me.

290
00:18:27,315 --> 00:18:29,233
Don't tell anyone where we're going.

291
00:18:29,442 --> 00:18:30,526
Keep this strictly confidential.

292
00:18:31,068 --> 00:18:32,193
"Strictly confidential"?

293
00:18:32,194 --> 00:18:34,572
KEEP THIS STRICTLY CONFIDENTIAL

294
00:18:35,489 --> 00:18:40,077
So, is it just Mr. Kang and me going?

295
00:18:42,371 --> 00:18:45,041
- Ms. Nam, hop in.
- Yes, sir.

296
00:18:54,216 --> 00:18:58,512
Anyway, why are we keeping
this business trip a secret?

297
00:18:58,929 --> 00:19:00,598
SE tricked us once.

298
00:19:01,223 --> 00:19:02,975
They may do it again.

299
00:19:03,726 --> 00:19:05,603
I want to keep this under the radar

300
00:19:06,020 --> 00:19:07,104
until the contract is signed.

301
00:19:09,398 --> 00:19:12,568
Fair enough. Even we don't know
where the master is.

302
00:19:12,818 --> 00:19:14,403
It'd be hard for them
to steal the item.

303
00:19:14,862 --> 00:19:17,573
But why are you taking me with you?

304
00:19:20,826 --> 00:19:23,245
You have the closest link
to the master.

305
00:19:24,830 --> 00:19:25,873
And more importantly

306
00:19:26,415 --> 00:19:28,000
you're the only one

307
00:19:29,126 --> 00:19:30,419
I can trust right now.

308
00:19:38,969 --> 00:19:41,722
Says someone
who once called me a spy.

309
00:19:43,099 --> 00:19:45,433
You can count on me.

310
00:19:45,434 --> 00:19:47,727
I, Nam Da-reum, will take full charge

311
00:19:47,728 --> 00:19:49,480
of escorting you around Jungsan-si.

312
00:19:58,989 --> 00:20:01,449
Please take good care of it.

313
00:20:01,450 --> 00:20:02,827
Thank you. Bye.

314
00:20:04,954 --> 00:20:07,664
I just got off the phone
with the natural silk thread place.

315
00:20:07,665 --> 00:20:09,666
We'll have samples by tomorrow.

316
00:20:09,667 --> 00:20:13,169
Brainstorm some ideas
on how to turn this into a product.

317
00:20:13,170 --> 00:20:14,422
- Yes, ma'am.
- Got it.

318
00:20:16,882 --> 00:20:18,925
Where did Ms. Da-reum go

319
00:20:18,926 --> 00:20:21,595
to find that master knot artisan?

320
00:20:21,929 --> 00:20:24,890
Did Mr. Kang go with her?

321
00:20:26,142 --> 00:20:29,061
Beats me. I'm not sure
about the details either.

322
00:20:30,229 --> 00:20:31,230
I see.

323
00:20:54,628 --> 00:20:55,880
I can't believe
we're passing by here.

324
00:20:57,381 --> 00:20:59,425
Over there is where I lived.

325
00:20:59,717 --> 00:21:02,470
Down this way is the market.

326
00:21:04,263 --> 00:21:05,890
If you head that way,
there's a lake park.

327
00:21:08,058 --> 00:21:10,352
You really do know
your way around here.

328
00:21:11,103 --> 00:21:12,771
Of course.

329
00:21:12,772 --> 00:21:15,816
You're practically a spy if you don't
know my name around here.

330
00:21:27,787 --> 00:21:29,246
Is that Nam Da-reum...

331
00:21:30,831 --> 00:21:32,249
the same Nam Da-reum
standing right here?

332
00:21:33,459 --> 00:21:34,542
NEULPUM CREDIT UNION MEMBER

333
00:21:34,543 --> 00:21:36,127
KIM MI-JA'S ELDEST DAUGHTER,
NAM DA-REUM

334
00:21:36,128 --> 00:21:37,254
JOINS SE CORPORATION!

335
00:21:39,173 --> 00:21:40,174
What is that?

336
00:21:41,133 --> 00:21:44,261
You really are a local celebrity.

337
00:21:45,429 --> 00:21:47,097
I can't believe this.

338
00:21:53,103 --> 00:21:54,188
Mo...

339
00:21:54,980 --> 00:21:56,065
Mom.

340
00:21:56,565 --> 00:21:58,984
What's with that banner?
Take it down right away.

341
00:21:59,276 --> 00:22:02,445
I paid good money for that,
so why would I take it down?

342
00:22:02,446 --> 00:22:04,990
It will stay up there
for at least half a year.

343
00:22:06,116 --> 00:22:07,284
I guess you've arrived.

344
00:22:07,451 --> 00:22:08,868
Aren't you coming to see me?

345
00:22:08,869 --> 00:22:10,746
I'm here for work,
so I won't be able to visit.

346
00:22:11,539 --> 00:22:13,123
What about the favor I asked for?

347
00:22:13,916 --> 00:22:16,710
Go to your old high school.

348
00:22:17,086 --> 00:22:19,087
She can only spare
a brief time after lunch.

349
00:22:19,088 --> 00:22:20,673
Got it.

350
00:22:21,298 --> 00:22:23,216
Thank you so much.

351
00:22:23,217 --> 00:22:24,468
I'll call you later.

352
00:22:25,010 --> 00:22:26,053
Bye.

353
00:22:29,348 --> 00:22:31,934
Don't take a picture of that.
Why would you even photograph it?

354
00:22:33,727 --> 00:22:35,521
You are the pride
of this entire town.

355
00:22:36,438 --> 00:22:37,940
Ms. Nam Da-reum

356
00:22:38,691 --> 00:22:40,025
of SE Corporation.

357
00:22:53,873 --> 00:22:55,082
If we go straight this way...

358
00:22:56,417 --> 00:22:58,210
- Isn't it pretty?
- This...

359
00:23:02,089 --> 00:23:04,425
This whole neighborhood
must be full of memories for you.

360
00:23:04,967 --> 00:23:06,051
Right.

361
00:23:07,052 --> 00:23:10,180
It feels a bit weird
to be here with you, though.

362
00:23:14,184 --> 00:23:15,519
That's my all-time
favorite snack bar!

363
00:23:16,979 --> 00:23:18,188
OUR SNACK FOOD

364
00:23:20,232 --> 00:23:22,026
Wow, I used to go there all the time.

365
00:23:31,785 --> 00:23:32,912
Stay on the inside.

366
00:23:34,163 --> 00:23:35,247
Okay.

367
00:23:40,419 --> 00:23:43,297
He's oddly sweet.

368
00:23:47,718 --> 00:23:49,886
Have a seat and wait for a moment.

369
00:23:49,887 --> 00:23:51,930
I'll call the cafeteria.

370
00:23:51,931 --> 00:23:55,142
- Okay, thank you.
- Thank you.

371
00:23:55,976 --> 00:23:57,686
- This way.
- Okay.

372
00:24:08,572 --> 00:24:09,823
It's been such a long time.

373
00:24:11,742 --> 00:24:13,118
Should we sit here for a bit?

374
00:24:16,956 --> 00:24:18,540
So, this is your old high school?

375
00:24:19,083 --> 00:24:20,167
Yes.

376
00:24:49,238 --> 00:24:50,614
I used to sit right here

377
00:24:51,865 --> 00:24:53,575
and listen to music a lot.

378
00:24:54,994 --> 00:24:56,370
Nothing has changed.

379
00:24:59,331 --> 00:25:01,041
- You're handsome.
- You're so handsome.

380
00:25:02,167 --> 00:25:04,043
- Hello.
- Are you a celebrity?

381
00:25:04,044 --> 00:25:05,712
- No.
- An actor? Or a model?

382
00:25:05,713 --> 00:25:08,256
You're so handsome.
Do you have Instar?

383
00:25:08,257 --> 00:25:09,424
Let's take a selfie.

384
00:25:09,425 --> 00:25:11,427
- Right here.
- You're seriously good-looking.

385
00:25:12,594 --> 00:25:14,137
- Awesome.
- So handsome.

386
00:25:14,138 --> 00:25:15,471
- Girls?
- Jeez.

387
00:25:15,472 --> 00:25:17,766
- I'm not anyone like that.
- You're so hot!

388
00:25:22,396 --> 00:25:23,564
What the heck?

389
00:25:23,856 --> 00:25:25,107
- Where are you going?
- What...

390
00:25:49,631 --> 00:25:51,925
Wait. Isn't that Da-reum?

391
00:25:52,468 --> 00:25:54,719
Hi, guys. Today, I'm going

392
00:25:54,720 --> 00:25:57,973
to vlog myself getting ready
to buy some wholesale stock.

393
00:25:58,557 --> 00:26:00,475
ASEUL-ASEUL
CLICK TO VISIT THE WEBSITE

394
00:26:00,476 --> 00:26:02,144
I don't drive

395
00:26:02,644 --> 00:26:05,064
so I'm taking a cab to get my stock.

396
00:26:05,439 --> 00:26:07,148
LIKE, COMMENT, AND SUBSCRIBE!

397
00:26:07,149 --> 00:26:10,526
This is the place I got
those strawberry panties from.

398
00:26:10,527 --> 00:26:12,695
I'm going for some daring panties
this time.

399
00:26:12,696 --> 00:26:14,030
I prefer to buy products

400
00:26:14,031 --> 00:26:16,199
after seeing and touching them
in person.

401
00:26:16,200 --> 00:26:17,784
You have all of those in stock.

402
00:26:17,785 --> 00:26:19,661
HIGH DEMAND EXPECTED
BLINK AND IT'S SOLD OUT

403
00:26:23,499 --> 00:26:25,334
I told you to keep it down
while I'm recording.

404
00:26:28,170 --> 00:26:30,255
Why aren't you doing
any actual work lately?

405
00:26:32,091 --> 00:26:33,467
I am working.

406
00:26:34,468 --> 00:26:37,679
I'm telling you. Video marketing is
how you sell these days.

407
00:26:38,097 --> 00:26:40,807
Wait and see.
Orders are going to pour in soon.

408
00:26:40,808 --> 00:26:42,266
As if.

409
00:26:42,267 --> 00:26:44,895
Refunds rather poured in
for those super push-up bras.

410
00:26:46,105 --> 00:26:47,147
Hey.

411
00:26:47,523 --> 00:26:49,398
I got scammed
because I was a newbie back then.

412
00:26:49,399 --> 00:26:52,069
How was I supposed to know
the padding would slide to the side?

413
00:26:53,570 --> 00:26:55,947
Which is why you should stick
to what you know.

414
00:26:55,948 --> 00:26:58,282
Why sell sexy lingerie
you've never even tried on?

415
00:26:58,283 --> 00:26:59,742
You fool.

416
00:26:59,743 --> 00:27:00,911
Darn you.

417
00:27:05,457 --> 00:27:07,042
Looks like I got an order.

418
00:27:09,294 --> 00:27:11,588
BYEOL-A

419
00:27:12,297 --> 00:27:14,507
BYEOL-A

420
00:27:14,508 --> 00:27:16,217
I guess Da-reum went down
to our hometown.

421
00:27:16,218 --> 00:27:17,219
What?

422
00:27:18,178 --> 00:27:19,971
- Without saying a word to us?
- You're right.

423
00:27:19,972 --> 00:27:23,266
Da-reum showed up at school
with a handsome guy.

424
00:27:23,267 --> 00:27:24,643
Maybe it's her boyfriend.

425
00:27:27,855 --> 00:27:28,856
Her boyfriend?

426
00:27:30,941 --> 00:27:33,944
Who was this tall, good-looking guy?

427
00:27:40,033 --> 00:27:43,495
You're incredibly popular
with those high school girls.

428
00:27:44,872 --> 00:27:46,874
I bet you broke a few hearts
back in your school days.

429
00:27:48,584 --> 00:27:51,378
Well, I suppose I had my moments.

430
00:27:54,548 --> 00:27:55,632
As always

431
00:27:56,049 --> 00:27:58,719
you're so honest.

432
00:28:00,262 --> 00:28:01,263
What about you?

433
00:28:02,639 --> 00:28:04,850
How were your school days?

434
00:28:07,644 --> 00:28:08,687
Make a guess.

435
00:28:10,522 --> 00:28:12,399
I guess you were bright

436
00:28:13,317 --> 00:28:14,359
energetic...

437
00:28:16,195 --> 00:28:18,822
and a total social butterfly
like you are now.

438
00:28:21,450 --> 00:28:22,492
Wrong.

439
00:28:23,952 --> 00:28:25,078
I was actually...

440
00:28:27,456 --> 00:28:28,957
an outcast for a while.

441
00:28:33,128 --> 00:28:34,504
I spent many lunch breaks

442
00:28:35,380 --> 00:28:37,591
sitting entirely on my own.

443
00:28:38,634 --> 00:28:39,635
That's why

444
00:28:40,385 --> 00:28:41,970
seeing kids like that earlier...

445
00:28:44,056 --> 00:28:45,265
tugs at me.

446
00:28:52,898 --> 00:28:54,942
It's a feeling only those
who have lived it can understand.

447
00:28:56,485 --> 00:28:57,819
Perhaps that's why

448
00:28:58,987 --> 00:29:01,573
you're so quick to care...

449
00:29:03,825 --> 00:29:04,868
for others.

450
00:29:10,165 --> 00:29:11,166
Still, I have

451
00:29:11,792 --> 00:29:14,169
way more good memories here.

452
00:29:14,419 --> 00:29:16,380
I found someone who gave me strength.

453
00:29:16,672 --> 00:29:17,881
I got through it fine thanks to him.

454
00:29:19,049 --> 00:29:20,300
Who was that?

455
00:29:23,428 --> 00:29:24,680
My...

456
00:29:26,765 --> 00:29:27,808
first love.

457
00:29:31,353 --> 00:29:33,521
Seeing how hard he tried

458
00:29:33,522 --> 00:29:37,025
motivated me to push myself harder.

459
00:29:37,943 --> 00:29:40,988
Anyway, I'm really grateful to him.

460
00:29:45,117 --> 00:29:46,159
That's a relief.

461
00:29:48,412 --> 00:29:49,663
I'm glad you had

462
00:29:50,872 --> 00:29:52,374
someone like that back then.

463
00:30:03,427 --> 00:30:05,012
Excuse me.

464
00:30:07,723 --> 00:30:10,057
Are you here to meet my master?

465
00:30:10,058 --> 00:30:11,393
Oh, yes.

466
00:30:11,893 --> 00:30:14,229
- Hello.
- Hello.

467
00:30:15,063 --> 00:30:16,523
NAM DA-REUM
KANG HA-GI

468
00:30:17,274 --> 00:30:20,318
I came out
because Mi-ja begged me, but...

469
00:30:20,319 --> 00:30:21,528
Just give us the location.

470
00:30:21,862 --> 00:30:23,488
We'll handle the talking.

471
00:30:24,698 --> 00:30:27,074
Promise never to mention
that you heard from me.

472
00:30:27,075 --> 00:30:28,451
Of course, we promise.

473
00:30:28,452 --> 00:30:32,539
It won't be easy.
Try to hold your ground. Good luck.

474
00:30:43,675 --> 00:30:45,927
Excuse me. Anyone here?

475
00:30:52,517 --> 00:30:54,686
- Hello.
- Hello.

476
00:31:11,620 --> 00:31:14,623
Hello. May I ask
where we can find the master?

477
00:31:15,165 --> 00:31:16,749
She's inside over there.

478
00:31:16,750 --> 00:31:18,460
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

479
00:31:23,256 --> 00:31:26,927
Wow, look at that color.
It turned out amazing.

480
00:31:27,844 --> 00:31:29,762
- Yeong-suk, grab some green onions.
- Okay.

481
00:31:29,763 --> 00:31:31,640
- Hello.
- Hello.

482
00:31:33,683 --> 00:31:34,684
Who are you?

483
00:31:35,560 --> 00:31:38,104
We're from a company
called Appello in Seoul.

484
00:31:38,105 --> 00:31:40,022
This is
Master Im Cheong-rim's place, right?

485
00:31:40,023 --> 00:31:42,734
Oh, my. How did you find this place?

486
00:31:44,945 --> 00:31:47,780
Cheong-rim! You have visitors.

487
00:31:47,781 --> 00:31:48,865
Come out and see.

488
00:32:19,938 --> 00:32:22,023
CERTIFICATE OF APPOINTMENT
SKILL TRANSMISSION MERIT AWARD

489
00:32:32,742 --> 00:32:36,745
Master Im, this is a mockup
we've prepared.

490
00:32:36,746 --> 00:32:37,789
BLENDING TRADITION WITH TRENDS

491
00:32:42,711 --> 00:32:47,048
Appello is a fashion platform
that curates local designer brands.

492
00:32:47,340 --> 00:32:48,924
Right now,
we're spearheading an initiative

493
00:32:48,925 --> 00:32:50,469
to merge traditional crafts
with modern design.

494
00:32:51,761 --> 00:32:54,388
We believe we can help
show your work to the world...

495
00:32:54,389 --> 00:32:55,682
What about the manufacturing?

496
00:32:55,891 --> 00:32:57,058
Please don't worry about that.

497
00:32:57,684 --> 00:32:59,686
We've got
a highly skilled factory lined up...

498
00:33:01,897 --> 00:33:03,190
A factory?

499
00:33:05,358 --> 00:33:06,443
I'm not interested.

500
00:33:08,570 --> 00:33:10,321
If you're not happy

501
00:33:10,322 --> 00:33:11,656
- with the factory...
- No.

502
00:33:11,865 --> 00:33:14,117
I have no words for merchants.

503
00:33:16,703 --> 00:33:17,954
Get out now.

504
00:33:32,302 --> 00:33:33,762
What now?

505
00:33:37,057 --> 00:33:39,184
Ms. Nam, you've done enough here.

506
00:33:39,976 --> 00:33:42,312
I'll drop you off at the bus terminal
so head back to Seoul without me.

507
00:33:43,230 --> 00:33:44,523
What about you, sir?

508
00:33:46,733 --> 00:33:48,485
I'm not leaving
until I convince Master Im.

509
00:33:49,528 --> 00:33:52,197
I became certain
after seeing her in person.

510
00:33:56,743 --> 00:33:57,827
Then...

511
00:33:58,870 --> 00:34:00,247
I'll stay too.

512
00:34:01,206 --> 00:34:02,541
I'll do whatever I can to help.

513
00:34:03,625 --> 00:34:04,668
What are you going to do?

514
00:34:08,255 --> 00:34:10,257
I should do whatever I can.

515
00:34:13,218 --> 00:34:14,219
Ms. Da-reum.

516
00:34:22,143 --> 00:34:25,437
We Koreans look out for each other.

517
00:34:25,438 --> 00:34:27,648
You're making a mountain of kimchi.

518
00:34:27,649 --> 00:34:28,816
How could I just walk away?

519
00:34:28,817 --> 00:34:30,569
Let me help out just a little.

520
00:34:30,860 --> 00:34:33,405
Should I season
the pickled napa cabbage?

521
00:34:34,823 --> 00:34:38,117
Your arms are as thin
as a pair of chopsticks.

522
00:34:38,118 --> 00:34:39,411
Have you made kimchi before?

523
00:34:40,078 --> 00:34:41,580
It's not an easy feat.

524
00:34:43,081 --> 00:34:45,457
I may not look it,
but I helped my mom

525
00:34:45,458 --> 00:34:47,210
for a good few years.

526
00:34:51,047 --> 00:34:53,216
- Pitch in already.
- Okay.

527
00:34:55,719 --> 00:34:57,428
Make sure to coat the outsides.

528
00:34:57,429 --> 00:34:59,014
- Like this?
- Spread it out.

529
00:35:00,682 --> 00:35:03,476
A farmhand from Seoul
is willing to help out.

530
00:35:03,768 --> 00:35:04,811
- What?
- Gosh...

531
00:35:05,270 --> 00:35:06,604
- A farmhand?
- How cute.

532
00:35:06,605 --> 00:35:09,440
- That looks heavy. Give me that.
- Don't be too eager.

533
00:35:09,441 --> 00:35:10,525
It looks heavy.

534
00:35:14,904 --> 00:35:16,071
The napa cabbages are pickled.

535
00:35:16,072 --> 00:35:17,282
He has chopsticks for arms too.

536
00:35:18,074 --> 00:35:19,701
- He's pretty useful, though.
- They go here?

537
00:35:20,452 --> 00:35:23,288
You have chopstick arms
and so does he.

538
00:35:23,955 --> 00:35:25,206
You look too weak.

539
00:35:25,540 --> 00:35:27,250
- He'll be of use somewhere.
- Give me that.

540
00:35:27,792 --> 00:35:29,294
Can he even lift chopsticks to eat?

541
00:35:30,587 --> 00:35:31,713
EYES ONLY FOR YOU, PARK SEO-JIN

542
00:35:35,842 --> 00:35:39,095
Push, push, push it away

543
00:35:39,429 --> 00:35:42,223
Push away the dirt in your heart

544
00:35:45,060 --> 00:35:46,227
To the beat.

545
00:35:47,020 --> 00:35:48,854
Did you tell Da-reum where to go?

546
00:35:48,855 --> 00:35:49,981
You bet.

547
00:35:50,440 --> 00:35:51,982
She was with a coworker.

548
00:35:51,983 --> 00:35:53,192
They looked really busy.

549
00:35:53,193 --> 00:35:54,485
- Right?
- Yes.

550
00:35:54,486 --> 00:35:57,029
Working at that huge company in Seoul

551
00:35:57,030 --> 00:35:58,657
must be really hard on her.

552
00:35:59,157 --> 00:36:02,993
She works at SE Corporation
of all places.

553
00:36:02,994 --> 00:36:05,454
- There must be lots to do.
- SE Corporation?

554
00:36:05,455 --> 00:36:07,832
That's weird. It wasn't called that.

555
00:36:09,584 --> 00:36:10,627
What do you mean?

556
00:36:11,002 --> 00:36:12,128
It wasn't called SE?

557
00:36:12,629 --> 00:36:14,172
- Pell-something.
- What?

558
00:36:14,464 --> 00:36:15,590
Pell...

559
00:36:15,924 --> 00:36:18,301
It sounded like pell... Oh, right.

560
00:36:20,637 --> 00:36:23,014
Appello. That's where she works.

561
00:36:24,307 --> 00:36:26,100
APPELLO
NAM DA-REUM

562
00:36:26,101 --> 00:36:27,102
What's this?

563
00:36:28,103 --> 00:36:29,521
"Appello"?

564
00:36:44,411 --> 00:36:45,829
- Ms. Da-reum.
- Yes?

565
00:36:46,287 --> 00:36:47,330
Do better.

566
00:36:47,706 --> 00:36:50,625
You're not supposed to smack it.
You're coating the leaves.

567
00:36:50,917 --> 00:36:53,586
Follow the grain
so it gets everywhere.

568
00:36:54,295 --> 00:36:55,380
So it seeps in.

569
00:36:57,674 --> 00:37:00,176
Like this? Is this what you do?

570
00:37:00,802 --> 00:37:02,804
You crushed all the leaves.

571
00:37:02,971 --> 00:37:04,513
Be more gentle.

572
00:37:04,514 --> 00:37:05,849
More caring, okay?

573
00:37:07,392 --> 00:37:11,020
You care about details
with everything.

574
00:37:11,396 --> 00:37:15,108
Once I set my mind to it,
I go all out.

575
00:37:24,701 --> 00:37:26,494
- I'm wearing this again.
- What?

576
00:37:28,580 --> 00:37:30,915
I thought the cast
would be the last of it.

577
00:37:33,960 --> 00:37:36,087
Wait. The red rubber gloves.

578
00:37:36,421 --> 00:37:38,548
Did you actually

579
00:37:39,466 --> 00:37:40,508
wear them?

580
00:37:48,308 --> 00:37:49,808
You burst into a fury and said

581
00:37:49,809 --> 00:37:52,770
you had to watch your back and front

582
00:37:52,771 --> 00:37:54,981
and that you couldn't
let your guard down.

583
00:37:56,608 --> 00:37:57,609
Did you wear them?

584
00:38:00,862 --> 00:38:02,989
I did wear them, okay?

585
00:38:03,448 --> 00:38:05,617
You swore you wouldn't.

586
00:38:05,867 --> 00:38:07,285
Jeez.

587
00:38:09,370 --> 00:38:10,580
Weren't they nice?

588
00:38:11,915 --> 00:38:12,999
Don't ask.

589
00:38:13,166 --> 00:38:15,834
- Do better.
- I am doing better.

590
00:38:15,835 --> 00:38:17,420
Your napa cabbage is almost...

591
00:38:17,754 --> 00:38:19,631
Mi-ja!

592
00:38:23,468 --> 00:38:24,469
Mom.

593
00:38:31,392 --> 00:38:32,894
What are you doing here?

594
00:38:38,358 --> 00:38:39,359
You!

595
00:38:40,819 --> 00:38:42,111
Give me those gloves.

596
00:38:43,112 --> 00:38:45,656
- What?
- Go over there

597
00:38:45,657 --> 00:38:47,658
and help move the kimchi.

598
00:38:47,659 --> 00:38:49,202
Give me the rubber gloves!

599
00:38:50,453 --> 00:38:51,830
Okay...

600
00:39:00,380 --> 00:39:01,464
Move.

601
00:39:06,511 --> 00:39:07,554
Mom...

602
00:39:10,682 --> 00:39:11,724
Master Im.

603
00:39:18,189 --> 00:39:19,482
Master Im.

604
00:39:20,400 --> 00:39:23,361
Please give my daughter a chance.

605
00:39:24,529 --> 00:39:26,865
She doesn't do a shoddy job,
whatever it is.

606
00:39:27,532 --> 00:39:30,577
With your help, she'll do great.

607
00:39:34,205 --> 00:39:35,540
The kimchi looks amazing.

608
00:39:36,332 --> 00:39:38,668
You bought
some quality napa cabbages.

609
00:39:39,294 --> 00:39:40,461
Look at the color.

610
00:39:43,506 --> 00:39:45,842
When you're done

611
00:39:46,259 --> 00:39:47,510
you need to wrap each head carefully.

612
00:39:48,052 --> 00:39:49,637
The more seasoning, the better.

613
00:39:57,812 --> 00:39:59,063
Look at you.

614
00:39:59,480 --> 00:40:00,773
You look good today.

615
00:40:02,025 --> 00:40:04,818
Should I not have registered
for a group lesson too?

616
00:40:04,819 --> 00:40:06,821
I can't have
all the ladies falling for me

617
00:40:07,196 --> 00:40:08,281
when Mi-mi's right there.

618
00:40:10,909 --> 00:40:13,327
Take a long step backward
with your right foot

619
00:40:13,328 --> 00:40:14,996
and go down and count one.

620
00:40:16,497 --> 00:40:17,540
Two.

621
00:40:18,374 --> 00:40:19,792
Again, one

622
00:40:21,044 --> 00:40:22,086
and two.

623
00:40:22,879 --> 00:40:24,255
Again, one.

624
00:40:24,881 --> 00:40:26,925
Arms forward, Mr. Min-woo.

625
00:40:27,175 --> 00:40:28,927
Strengthen your core.

626
00:40:29,093 --> 00:40:31,930
Keep your back straight
and strengthen your core.

627
00:40:32,847 --> 00:40:34,056
Watch your core.

628
00:40:34,057 --> 00:40:36,892
Keep your arms down
and watch your core.

629
00:40:36,893 --> 00:40:39,896
That's it. Keep this posture. Two.

630
00:40:41,189 --> 00:40:43,315
Again, one.

631
00:40:43,316 --> 00:40:45,275
Breathe in and straighten your back.

632
00:40:45,276 --> 00:40:47,320
Your arms should be up here.

633
00:40:48,112 --> 00:40:50,990
Why are you so weak?

634
00:40:51,658 --> 00:40:53,117
And two.

635
00:40:53,660 --> 00:40:55,578
- Get back up, Mr. Min-woo.
- Okay.

636
00:40:56,955 --> 00:40:59,540
This is the last count. One...

637
00:41:03,628 --> 00:41:06,089
SMOOTH PILATES

638
00:41:06,422 --> 00:41:08,091
- What, really?
- Yes.

639
00:41:11,052 --> 00:41:12,720
Don't be silly.

640
00:41:15,014 --> 00:41:16,307
Oh, my gosh.

641
00:41:16,933 --> 00:41:17,976
Min-woo.

642
00:41:18,768 --> 00:41:21,269
Come here. We're leaving.

643
00:41:21,270 --> 00:41:22,813
Where to?

644
00:41:22,814 --> 00:41:24,064
Where else?

645
00:41:24,065 --> 00:41:26,149
To your welcome dinner, of course.

646
00:41:26,150 --> 00:41:28,235
- I don't need one.
- Let's go.

647
00:41:28,236 --> 00:41:29,487
- Come along.
- But I...

648
00:41:30,196 --> 00:41:32,114
- What do you like?
- Goodbye.

649
00:41:32,115 --> 00:41:33,699
- Meat.
- You're not coming?

650
00:41:33,700 --> 00:41:35,284
- Bye.
- See you.

651
00:41:42,792 --> 00:41:44,419
- Take this, please.
- Sure.

652
00:41:44,919 --> 00:41:46,004
Oh, dear.

653
00:41:47,130 --> 00:41:48,256
It's so hot.

654
00:41:50,925 --> 00:41:53,761
- Ms. Da-reum. I'll take it.
- Thanks.

655
00:41:56,180 --> 00:41:57,723
Where did Mi-ja go?

656
00:41:57,724 --> 00:42:01,728
- Tell your mom dinner's ready.
- Okay.

657
00:42:13,322 --> 00:42:14,323
Mom.

658
00:42:33,009 --> 00:42:35,011
Thanks for your help.

659
00:42:37,138 --> 00:42:38,973
After all I went through
to raise you...

660
00:42:42,351 --> 00:42:46,355
What work do you do
that you're here making kimchi?

661
00:42:50,401 --> 00:42:52,487
Mom, actually...

662
00:42:53,946 --> 00:42:55,907
There's something I didn't tell you.

663
00:42:58,659 --> 00:42:59,660
I...

664
00:43:03,790 --> 00:43:06,584
I quit SE Corporation.

665
00:43:08,753 --> 00:43:09,754
I know.

666
00:43:12,840 --> 00:43:15,634
- You know?
- It's Appello or something.

667
00:43:15,635 --> 00:43:16,719
I saw your business card.

668
00:43:23,893 --> 00:43:25,478
I'm sorry I lied.

669
00:43:27,396 --> 00:43:30,274
You were so pleased
that I got into SE Corporation.

670
00:43:30,733 --> 00:43:32,735
I didn't want to let you down.

671
00:43:33,402 --> 00:43:37,323
I'm not upset
that you left a huge corporation.

672
00:43:41,160 --> 00:43:42,829
You didn't tell me.

673
00:43:43,996 --> 00:43:45,289
That's what hurts.

674
00:43:48,751 --> 00:43:51,795
Wouldn't it have been nice
if you'd told me

675
00:43:51,796 --> 00:43:54,257
you were having
a hard time at school?

676
00:43:55,007 --> 00:43:57,135
I know it's because
you don't want me to worry

677
00:43:59,137 --> 00:44:01,889
but I wonder
if it's because you don't trust me.

678
00:44:03,808 --> 00:44:06,519
Each time you keep something from me

679
00:44:09,105 --> 00:44:10,439
I get really upset.

680
00:44:21,242 --> 00:44:22,410
I'm sorry.

681
00:44:24,245 --> 00:44:25,538
I won't do it again.

682
00:44:30,793 --> 00:44:31,919
But Mom.

683
00:44:32,253 --> 00:44:34,380
It's a small company

684
00:44:34,797 --> 00:44:38,801
but they use my ideas,
and I can voice my opinion.

685
00:44:39,927 --> 00:44:41,012
I feel...

686
00:44:43,639 --> 00:44:46,559
like I can be of use there.

687
00:44:47,101 --> 00:44:49,353
That's why I like Appello

688
00:44:51,439 --> 00:44:53,274
and I'm happier there.

689
00:45:02,158 --> 00:45:03,492
Then all is well.

690
00:45:04,243 --> 00:45:07,163
Whether you work at a big
or a small company, all I want...

691
00:45:09,540 --> 00:45:11,000
is for you to be happy.

692
00:45:24,847 --> 00:45:26,474
Thank you, Mom.

693
00:45:37,902 --> 00:45:38,986
Don't cry.

694
00:45:51,749 --> 00:45:53,834
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

695
00:45:54,669 --> 00:45:56,419
- You too?
- How is it?

696
00:45:56,420 --> 00:45:58,339
- I'll get more meat.
- Okay.

697
00:46:00,841 --> 00:46:02,927
Ma'am, have some of this.

698
00:46:03,928 --> 00:46:05,096
And this.

699
00:46:06,013 --> 00:46:07,181
Thanks.

700
00:46:11,978 --> 00:46:13,312
My Da-reum.

701
00:46:13,938 --> 00:46:15,523
Look after her for me, Mr. Kang.

702
00:46:16,065 --> 00:46:17,983
She hasn't worked for that long

703
00:46:17,984 --> 00:46:19,944
so she has a lot to learn.

704
00:46:20,444 --> 00:46:21,570
Not a lot, actually.

705
00:46:22,363 --> 00:46:23,406
Just a bit.

706
00:46:24,407 --> 00:46:25,408
She lacks just a bit.

707
00:46:26,784 --> 00:46:29,078
She's diligent
and hard-working, though.

708
00:46:29,412 --> 00:46:30,997
All my employees work hard.

709
00:46:35,751 --> 00:46:37,712
I guess you have nothing good

710
00:46:38,087 --> 00:46:40,256
to say about my Da-reum.

711
00:46:44,051 --> 00:46:45,177
Ms. Da-reum

712
00:46:46,220 --> 00:46:47,596
is an exemplary employee.

713
00:46:50,016 --> 00:46:51,392
She's always so cheerful

714
00:46:51,851 --> 00:46:53,727
and she gives every task her all.

715
00:46:53,728 --> 00:46:57,398
She hasn't been with us very long,
but she's already been a huge help.

716
00:46:58,357 --> 00:46:59,775
You don't have to worry.

717
00:47:01,610 --> 00:47:03,904
My gosh. Is that so?

718
00:47:05,406 --> 00:47:08,743
I thought she was kind
and warmhearted.

719
00:47:09,285 --> 00:47:11,871
She must've gotten that from you.

720
00:47:14,665 --> 00:47:15,666
What?

721
00:47:16,250 --> 00:47:17,626
How did you know that?

722
00:47:18,377 --> 00:47:22,714
People say we're carbon copies
whenever we're out together.

723
00:47:22,715 --> 00:47:24,758
- Do they?
- Oh, let's clink bowls.

724
00:47:24,759 --> 00:47:25,760
Sure.

725
00:47:33,768 --> 00:47:36,937
You're a good drinker, Mr. Kang.

726
00:47:37,938 --> 00:47:39,440
- Have some more.
- Thanks.

727
00:47:43,819 --> 00:47:44,862
Gosh.

728
00:47:46,030 --> 00:47:47,615
- You too.
- Thanks.

729
00:47:50,034 --> 00:47:52,911
So, about my Da-reum.

730
00:47:52,912 --> 00:47:55,414
Is she seeing anyone at work?

731
00:47:57,124 --> 00:47:58,417
Or have a crush on someone?

732
00:47:59,293 --> 00:48:00,378
Pardon?

733
00:48:02,380 --> 00:48:04,548
I don't know anything about that.

734
00:48:06,008 --> 00:48:09,887
I'm worried. She doesn't seem
to care about dating.

735
00:48:13,808 --> 00:48:14,850
By the way

736
00:48:15,309 --> 00:48:17,770
you look incredibly young.

737
00:48:18,396 --> 00:48:21,816
Are you still unmarried?

738
00:48:22,608 --> 00:48:25,361
Unmarried? Yes, I am.

739
00:48:27,279 --> 00:48:28,364
Are you?

740
00:48:30,741 --> 00:48:31,742
Then

741
00:48:31,992 --> 00:48:35,704
what is your ideal kind of woman?

742
00:48:36,414 --> 00:48:37,706
- Pardon?
- You said

743
00:48:37,915 --> 00:48:40,251
Da-reum was kind and warmhearted.

744
00:48:41,043 --> 00:48:43,963
Are you not into that kind of woman?

745
00:48:44,380 --> 00:48:46,006
Well, it's not...

746
00:48:47,591 --> 00:48:48,717
Mom.

747
00:48:49,802 --> 00:48:51,636
Why are you talking nonsense?

748
00:48:51,637 --> 00:48:53,596
Don't grill my boss.

749
00:48:53,597 --> 00:48:57,851
I just wanted to know
what his ideal type was.

750
00:48:57,852 --> 00:49:00,353
You're not supposed to ask that
at work.

751
00:49:00,354 --> 00:49:01,980
There are reasons too.

752
00:49:01,981 --> 00:49:05,568
Did I just get you fired
when you just joined?

753
00:49:05,943 --> 00:49:07,695
- No way.
- What if I did?

754
00:49:07,903 --> 00:49:08,946
Ma'am.

755
00:49:09,738 --> 00:49:11,323
The man your daughter has a crush on.

756
00:49:12,700 --> 00:49:13,742
It's me.

757
00:49:16,996 --> 00:49:19,039
APPELLO

758
00:49:26,589 --> 00:49:28,007
Director.

759
00:49:28,716 --> 00:49:30,426
- Hello.
- Hello.

760
00:49:31,552 --> 00:49:33,470
What brings you here?

761
00:49:33,471 --> 00:49:35,014
I dropped by after a shoot.

762
00:49:35,723 --> 00:49:37,975
Is Marketing busy these days?

763
00:49:38,851 --> 00:49:42,021
The K-Wave project
keeps us here late every day.

764
00:49:46,108 --> 00:49:47,568
Mr. Ha-gi's still here, right?

765
00:49:48,027 --> 00:49:49,403
Mr. Kang's on a business trip.

766
00:49:52,615 --> 00:49:53,616
With Ms. Da-reum.

767
00:49:54,992 --> 00:49:55,993
With Ms. Da-reum?

768
00:49:57,077 --> 00:49:59,747
To sign with a master knot artisan
from Ms. Da-reum's hometown.

769
00:50:00,789 --> 00:50:02,624
They seem to be stuck.

770
00:50:02,625 --> 00:50:04,752
I don't think they'll return
until the deal is signed.

771
00:50:07,171 --> 00:50:08,546
We're ready for the meeting.

772
00:50:08,547 --> 00:50:09,673
- Okay.
- Great.

773
00:50:10,841 --> 00:50:13,301
Director, I have a meeting.

774
00:50:13,302 --> 00:50:14,386
What will you do?

775
00:50:16,972 --> 00:50:19,474
There's no one else here to see.
I'll get going.

776
00:50:19,475 --> 00:50:21,810
- Get back safely, Director.
- Take care.

777
00:50:43,040 --> 00:50:44,958
APPELLO
NAM DA-REUM

778
00:50:44,959 --> 00:50:47,294
MAP TO MOUNT NAMSAN LOCATION,
ROUTE AND EVENT COMMENTS

779
00:50:49,255 --> 00:50:51,757
K-WAVE PROJECT
APPELLO WILL WIN! LET'S GO!

780
00:51:07,523 --> 00:51:09,399
A fan of mine drew this character.

781
00:51:09,400 --> 00:51:11,234
It's so cute
that I've got it all memorized.

782
00:51:11,235 --> 00:51:12,903
MONTH-END MARKETING MEETING

783
00:51:33,549 --> 00:51:34,675
It was Da-reum.

784
00:51:38,512 --> 00:51:40,598
Will you really be okay
going home alone?

785
00:51:40,848 --> 00:51:43,225
You're here for work.

786
00:51:43,559 --> 00:51:47,353
Do your best
and win Master Im over, okay?

787
00:51:47,354 --> 00:51:50,106
- Okay. Get home safe, Mom.
- I will.

788
00:51:50,107 --> 00:51:53,861
- Get back safely, ma'am.
- Thank you, Mr. Kang.

789
00:51:54,028 --> 00:51:57,156
- Take care of my daughter for me.
- Don't.

790
00:51:57,323 --> 00:51:58,990
- Bye, Eun-jeong.
- Take care.

791
00:51:58,991 --> 00:52:00,784
- Bye, Mom.
- Bye.

792
00:52:01,660 --> 00:52:03,537
Get home safe.

793
00:52:12,880 --> 00:52:16,008
I'm pleased that you want to learn
how to make these.

794
00:52:16,759 --> 00:52:19,094
I've been doing it for over ten years
but I still find it tough.

795
00:52:19,470 --> 00:52:21,472
Master Im always says

796
00:52:21,680 --> 00:52:23,766
making knots is like
asceticism or meditation.

797
00:52:24,642 --> 00:52:27,144
She did it all her life
and she says it's still hard.

798
00:52:27,728 --> 00:52:30,314
Compared to her,
I barely learned how to walk.

799
00:52:31,440 --> 00:52:32,983
Maybe I'm yet to be born.

800
00:52:33,567 --> 00:52:36,152
Anyway, as you can see here

801
00:52:36,153 --> 00:52:39,822
this is a braided cord,
and it's covered in braided threads.

802
00:52:39,823 --> 00:52:42,576
I'll teach you
how to make a knot out of this.

803
00:52:43,410 --> 00:52:45,828
You must want to get a feel.

804
00:52:45,829 --> 00:52:48,082
Shall we sit over there?

805
00:52:50,209 --> 00:52:52,711
I'll teach you the easiest one.

806
00:52:53,379 --> 00:52:57,173
It's one of the basic knots
called dongsimgyeol.

807
00:52:57,174 --> 00:52:58,675
- Dongsimgyeol.
- Dongsimgyeol.

808
00:52:58,676 --> 00:53:00,927
First, make a knot loop.

809
00:53:00,928 --> 00:53:04,430
Knot loops are these large holes.

810
00:53:04,431 --> 00:53:06,850
Take the two strands that are hanging

811
00:53:07,142 --> 00:53:10,269
and put them between
the second and third loops.

812
00:53:10,270 --> 00:53:12,605
- Like this?
- That's perfect.

813
00:53:12,606 --> 00:53:14,191
You're doing well.

814
00:53:18,529 --> 00:53:20,030
And then...

815
00:53:21,281 --> 00:53:22,533
This one...

816
00:53:23,575 --> 00:53:26,828
This goes up and fold...

817
00:53:26,829 --> 00:53:29,623
Do I fold this one or that one?

818
00:53:30,541 --> 00:53:32,334
This... Hang on.

819
00:53:32,710 --> 00:53:34,795
You did it wrong.

820
00:53:38,924 --> 00:53:40,508
It's not like this.

821
00:53:40,509 --> 00:53:42,927
- This goes in here.
- Oh, that one?

822
00:53:42,928 --> 00:53:45,013
- That goes first?
- And then

823
00:53:45,681 --> 00:53:47,432
you slip this in here.

824
00:53:47,433 --> 00:53:49,016
- Oh, this...
- In here.

825
00:53:49,017 --> 00:53:51,520
- In the middle.
- Wait. Like this?

826
00:53:52,396 --> 00:53:54,815
It's done. Oh, like this?

827
00:54:37,649 --> 00:54:38,859
TRAINING COMPLETION CEREMONY

828
00:54:44,990 --> 00:54:47,826
We did it. It's done.

829
00:54:50,037 --> 00:54:51,955
After making this myself

830
00:54:52,664 --> 00:54:55,250
it looks extra pretty
and I'm so proud of it.

831
00:54:57,085 --> 00:54:58,128
It does.

832
00:54:59,713 --> 00:55:01,507
I get what she meant

833
00:55:01,924 --> 00:55:03,717
when she said it merges with time.

834
00:55:06,220 --> 00:55:09,389
I didn't know so much work
went into making such a small knot.

835
00:55:28,158 --> 00:55:29,701
I tried to manage on my own.

836
00:55:30,035 --> 00:55:31,411
Thank you.

837
00:55:32,246 --> 00:55:33,454
It's fine.

838
00:55:33,455 --> 00:55:35,415
Tell us if you need help
with anything.

839
00:55:36,708 --> 00:55:39,670
All my fellow students have left.

840
00:55:40,128 --> 00:55:43,048
I'm the last remaining successor.

841
00:55:44,299 --> 00:55:45,592
If I were to quit too

842
00:55:46,468 --> 00:55:47,845
this skill will die out.

843
00:55:55,060 --> 00:55:58,564
Please persuade Master Im for me.

844
00:56:01,900 --> 00:56:06,113
It's a matter of time
before we lose all the artisans.

845
00:56:07,072 --> 00:56:10,033
The work is intense,
and we barely make a living.

846
00:56:11,076 --> 00:56:12,119
Who would do this?

847
00:56:13,662 --> 00:56:15,621
Factory-made or handmade

848
00:56:15,622 --> 00:56:18,500
I just want people to know
about traditional knots.

849
00:56:24,756 --> 00:56:27,092
Is this what you thought all along?

850
00:56:27,843 --> 00:56:28,927
Master Im.

851
00:56:30,095 --> 00:56:31,597
If that's how you think, leave.

852
00:56:32,681 --> 00:56:35,559
Make knots at a factory
and make a fortune!

853
00:56:37,269 --> 00:56:38,437
"Make a fortune"?

854
00:56:40,147 --> 00:56:43,609
I'd have quit long ago
if that's what I wanted.

855
00:56:44,651 --> 00:56:47,863
I do this
to keep the tradition alive.

856
00:56:48,655 --> 00:56:50,449
We need all the help we can get.

857
00:56:50,908 --> 00:56:52,075
I at least...

858
00:56:54,494 --> 00:56:55,704
Why do you say

859
00:56:56,204 --> 00:56:58,040
I'm wrong just because

860
00:56:58,624 --> 00:57:00,626
I take a different approach
to protect it?

861
00:57:34,493 --> 00:57:35,535
Ms. Da-reum.

862
00:57:36,411 --> 00:57:38,038
Yes?

863
00:57:38,664 --> 00:57:41,249
Can you come outside?

864
00:57:43,377 --> 00:57:44,461
Give me a moment.

865
00:57:53,804 --> 00:57:56,807
I stuck them in the fire earlier
and didn't want to eat them alone.

866
00:57:57,307 --> 00:57:59,559
Roasted sweet potatoes.

867
00:58:00,227 --> 00:58:01,895
I didn't know you like this.

868
00:58:09,236 --> 00:58:10,821
Have a taste.

869
00:58:13,031 --> 00:58:15,367
- It smells amazing.
- Watch out. It's hot.

870
00:58:19,913 --> 00:58:21,373
Ms. Da-reum, are you all right?

871
00:58:23,250 --> 00:58:24,334
Spit it out here.

872
00:58:27,587 --> 00:58:30,298
Why is he holding out his hands?

873
00:58:31,425 --> 00:58:33,135
No, it's fine.

874
00:58:46,398 --> 00:58:47,816
Take your time. Don't hurt yourself.

875
00:58:49,109 --> 00:58:50,193
Thank you.

876
00:59:01,163 --> 00:59:04,958
Why is Mr. Kang so nice to me?

877
00:59:12,924 --> 00:59:14,342
It reminds me of my grandma.

878
00:59:15,844 --> 00:59:19,097
She used to roast me
sweet potatoes like this.

879
00:59:23,351 --> 00:59:24,519
It must be nice...

880
00:59:26,313 --> 00:59:28,231
to have a kind grandma

881
00:59:29,274 --> 00:59:30,567
and a mother.

882
00:59:33,695 --> 00:59:34,780
Thanks to you

883
00:59:35,697 --> 00:59:37,032
I enjoyed today.

884
00:59:38,492 --> 00:59:39,534
What did you enjoy?

885
00:59:43,663 --> 00:59:45,457
Drinking with your mother.

886
00:59:51,296 --> 00:59:53,090
My mom died when I was
a high-school senior.

887
00:59:55,425 --> 00:59:56,802
I never got to do that.

888
01:00:10,148 --> 01:00:13,193
You can scratch that
off your bucket list.

889
01:00:15,237 --> 01:00:16,321
I can.

890
01:00:19,616 --> 01:00:20,659
What about you?

891
01:00:21,409 --> 01:00:22,452
Do you have a bucket list?

892
01:00:28,125 --> 01:00:30,168
Sit in the front row at a concert?

893
01:00:31,711 --> 01:00:33,213
Have a pet?

894
01:00:33,588 --> 01:00:34,589
And to hear

895
01:00:35,590 --> 01:00:36,842
someone say to me

896
01:00:37,759 --> 01:00:42,305
that they're glad to have me around.

897
01:00:48,979 --> 01:00:50,564
It's corny, isn't it?

898
01:01:18,592 --> 01:01:19,843
I must've been by the fire
for too long.

899
01:01:21,845 --> 01:01:22,888
It's hot.

900
01:01:23,972 --> 01:01:25,849
- I'll take a stroll.
- Okay.

901
01:01:33,815 --> 01:01:34,816
What about you?

902
01:01:37,319 --> 01:01:38,320
Would you like

903
01:01:39,321 --> 01:01:40,322
to come with me on a walk?

904
01:01:49,789 --> 01:01:50,916
I have a feeling

905
01:01:52,834 --> 01:01:54,419
I'll remember today for a long time.

906
01:01:56,254 --> 01:01:57,255
Me too.

907
01:01:58,924 --> 01:02:00,383
I'm glad that you were here...

908
01:02:02,677 --> 01:02:03,803
with me.

909
01:02:09,100 --> 01:02:11,728
You took something off
my bucket list.

910
01:02:21,279 --> 01:02:22,405
Ms. Da-reum.

911
01:02:24,824 --> 01:02:26,368
You told me before

912
01:02:27,285 --> 01:02:28,620
that you joined Appello

913
01:02:30,330 --> 01:02:32,290
because there was someone
you wanted to meet.

914
01:02:35,835 --> 01:02:36,920
Yes, well...

915
01:02:37,337 --> 01:02:38,546
That was true then.

916
01:02:39,506 --> 01:02:42,342
What's going on?
Why is he asking me that?

917
01:02:42,801 --> 01:02:43,969
Be honest with me today.

918
01:02:46,846 --> 01:02:48,139
The person you wanted to meet.

919
01:02:49,182 --> 01:02:50,350
Was it me?

920
01:02:53,728 --> 01:02:54,729
Pardon?

921
01:02:57,524 --> 01:02:58,858
Do you see me as a man?

922
01:03:00,026 --> 01:03:02,988
Do you think

923
01:03:03,571 --> 01:03:07,701
that I'm interested in you?

924
01:03:10,120 --> 01:03:12,705
It's just us two here. We can be...

925
01:03:12,706 --> 01:03:13,707
No, wait.

926
01:03:14,332 --> 01:03:15,417
Just a moment.

927
01:03:15,917 --> 01:03:17,210
Is that why you said

928
01:03:17,544 --> 01:03:20,421
you were the CEO
and I was an employee

929
01:03:20,422 --> 01:03:21,965
and tried to keep your distance?

930
01:03:26,094 --> 01:03:28,430
Was that really the reason?

931
01:03:33,143 --> 01:03:38,064
I know very well
that we can never be.

932
01:03:38,898 --> 01:03:41,443
I know so well who you like.

933
01:03:44,195 --> 01:03:45,196
I did what?

934
01:03:48,783 --> 01:03:49,784
Who could that be?

935
01:03:52,454 --> 01:03:54,789
Oh, well...

936
01:04:00,128 --> 01:04:01,713
Who do I like?

937
01:04:10,680 --> 01:04:12,891
You have a thing
for Director Lee Chan.

938
01:04:13,308 --> 01:04:16,561
- What?
- For a long time.

939
01:04:19,439 --> 01:04:20,523
What the...

940
01:04:21,149 --> 01:04:22,566
Excuse me?

941
01:04:22,567 --> 01:04:24,235
Don't you worry.

942
01:04:24,402 --> 01:04:27,530
I'll guard your feelings for you.

943
01:04:27,822 --> 01:04:30,241
I'm not prejudiced at all.

944
01:04:34,788 --> 01:04:36,039
Wait, Ms. Da-reum.

945
01:04:36,956 --> 01:04:38,166
All this while

946
01:04:38,750 --> 01:04:42,253
you thought I liked men?

947
01:04:45,757 --> 01:04:46,841
But you do.

948
01:04:52,847 --> 01:04:54,099
Ms. Da-reum.

949
01:04:54,599 --> 01:04:56,309
I'm not into men.

950
01:04:57,352 --> 01:04:58,728
- What?
- Also...

951
01:05:00,605 --> 01:05:02,482
there's this woman
I'm interested in right now.

952
01:05:05,443 --> 01:05:06,444
What?

953
01:06:16,014 --> 01:06:19,934
MY BIAS, MY BOSS

954
01:06:30,737 --> 01:06:33,531
EPILOGUE

955
01:06:38,119 --> 01:06:39,245
Shall we pull?

956
01:06:41,164 --> 01:06:43,208
Oh, yes.

957
01:06:46,836 --> 01:06:47,962
It's done.

958
01:06:53,259 --> 01:06:54,677
Do you know how to do it now?

959
01:06:56,054 --> 01:06:58,181
Try it yourself.

960
01:07:05,688 --> 01:07:08,191
It's the first thing
we made together.

961
01:07:09,359 --> 01:07:11,194
Was it called dongsimgyeol?

962
01:07:19,577 --> 01:07:20,578
Why are you so surprised?

963
01:07:23,039 --> 01:07:24,040
I'm not.

964
01:07:38,555 --> 01:07:41,390
DONGSIMGYEOL KNOT

965
01:07:41,391 --> 01:07:43,392
TO BE OF ONE HEART FOREVER

966
01:07:43,393 --> 01:07:45,144
WISHES FOR ETERNAL LOVE AND PEACE

967
01:07:45,603 --> 01:07:47,397
Who is the woman he's interested in?

968
01:07:48,606 --> 01:07:50,942
- Let's go in my car.
- Come with me.

969
01:07:52,277 --> 01:07:53,860
What's this plot twist?

970
01:07:53,861 --> 01:07:55,696
"You're the woman I'm interested in."

971
01:07:55,697 --> 01:07:57,949
Why can't you say it? Why?

972
01:07:58,324 --> 01:08:02,036
How about we stay
by each other's side from now on?

973
01:08:04,539 --> 01:08:05,790
Who did she go to see?

974
01:08:06,416 --> 01:08:07,708
You're so handsome.

975
01:08:07,709 --> 01:08:10,253
- Don't be with a guy like that.
- Mr. Kang.

976
01:08:10,795 --> 01:08:13,339
It's okay to tell me
that you're not okay.

977
01:08:28,062 --> 01:08:30,064
Subtitles by Eunjin Erica Kim
and Jennifer Jean Lim
